JPurrr-8000 @VERSION@ - how to install
=====================================

JPurrr-8000 is a free and open source synth (VST3 plugin and standalone app).
This zip has one installer per system, the manual, and a checksum list.

  Windows/   JPurrr-8000-@VERSION@-Windows-x64-Setup.exe
  macOS/     JPurrr-8000-@VERSION@-macOS.pkg
  Linux/     JPurrr-8000-@VERSION@-Linux-x86_64.tar.gz
  JPurrr-8000-manual.pdf, SHA256SUMS.txt, LICENSE, this file

Use only the folder for your system. Close your DAW first, and rescan
plugins afterwards. Presets and settings are never removed by an uninstall.


WINDOWS 10 and 11 (64 bit)
--------------------------
1. Unzip, open the Windows folder and run the Setup.exe.
2. If Windows says "Windows protected your PC" (SmartScreen), click
   "More info", then "Run anyway".
3. The plugin goes to C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3 and the standalone
   app to C:\Program Files\Studio 87\JPurrr-8000.
   Uninstall in Settings, Apps.

Why the warning: the Setup is not code signed. A signing certificate costs
money every year and this project is free. The warning does not mean the
file is infected. It means Windows does not know the publisher. You can
check the file with SHA256SUMS.txt (see below).


MACOS 11 or newer (Apple silicon and Intel)
-------------------------------------------
The .pkg is not signed or notarized by Apple, so macOS blocks it the first
time ("Apple could not verify ... is free of malware"). It does not mean
the file is infected. It means Apple has not checked it.

Why: Apple only skips this warning for developers who pay for the Apple
Developer Program (99 US dollars per year). JPurrr-8000 is free software.

Easiest way, no warning: download the package with Terminal, because a
browser marks its downloads "from the internet" and that mark triggers the
block (and unzipping keeps the mark). Open Terminal and run:

  curl -L -o ~/Downloads/JPurrr-8000.pkg https://github.com/SpeakingColors/JPurrr-8000/releases/download/@TAG@/JPurrr-8000-@VERSION@-macOS.pkg
  open ~/Downloads/JPurrr-8000.pkg

If you use the .pkg from this zip: double click it, close the message, open
System Settings, Privacy & Security, scroll down and click "Open Anyway"
(the button stays for about an hour), then confirm with your password. If
the message comes back, run this in Terminal and open the file again:

  xattr -d com.apple.quarantine <path of the .pkg file>

On macOS 14 and older you can also right click the .pkg, choose Open, then
Open again. Only do this for files from the official release page.

The plugin goes to /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3 and the app to
/Applications. The uninstaller is uninstall.command in
/Library/Application Support/Studio 87/JPurrr-8000.
More: https://github.com/SpeakingColors/JPurrr-8000/blob/main/docs/macos-install.md


LINUX (x86_64)
--------------
1. Unpack the tar.gz in the Linux folder:
     tar -xzf JPurrr-8000-@VERSION@-Linux-x86_64.tar.gz
2. Open a terminal in the unpacked folder and run:
     ./install.sh
   It installs for your user only, no root needed: the plugin to ~/.vst3,
   the standalone app to ~/.local/bin, plus a menu entry.
   "./install.sh --dry-run" shows what it would do first.
3. To remove it again, run "./install.sh --uninstall".
   Or copy the JPurrr-8000.vst3 folder to ~/.vst3/ yourself.


CHECK YOUR DOWNLOAD
-------------------
SHA256SUMS.txt lists the SHA-256 checksum of every file in this zip.
Linux and macOS: in the unpacked folder run
  shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS.txt
Every line must say OK. Windows PowerShell:
  Get-FileHash .\Windows\JPurrr-8000-@VERSION@-Windows-x64-Setup.exe
and compare the result with the line in SHA256SUMS.txt.
The release page also has a SHA256SUMS.txt for the separate downloads.


